Currently, the main forming methods used in the industrial production of wood-plastic composite materials include extrusion molding, hot press molding, injection molding, and blow molding. With the further development of research and application of wood-plastic composite materials, it can be expected that their processing technology will have the following development trends:
① Diversification of raw material compounding;
② High loading of wood flour filling;
③ Specialization of equipment and processes;
④ Diversification of forming processes;
⑤ High-grade finished products.

Wood-plastic materials are currently divided into two major product categories based on application scenarios: outdoor and indoor. According to their uses, they can be classified into structural, decorative, packaging, and special types. According to their forms, they include wires, profiles, sheets, plates, and special-shaped materials, among others. Their application scope can almost cover all fields where wood, plastic, steel-plastic, aluminum alloys, and other similar composite materials are currently used. It is reported that some wood-plastic materials were used in the 2004 Athens Olympic Games, and this new material was also used in the Beijing Olympic Games.

At present, the selling price of 1 ton of high-quality wood-plastic materials is about 10,000 yuan, while 1 ton of common structural wood-plastic materials can replace approximately 2 to 2.5 cubic meters of wood (this is the maximum timber yield of one mu of forest in one year), and the price per cubic meter is less than 5,000 yuan. The price of ordinary-quality wood-plastic materials may even be lower, making them completely acceptable to the market.
